---
description: Thrum session lifecycle protocol
alwaysApply: true
---
At session start, run `thrum prime` to load identity and context.
Before compaction, the coordinator runs the update-project workflow when it owns project state.
Other agents save a restart snapshot before any restart, and keep state and queue current.
Check `thrum inbox --unread` for pending messages from other agents.
- Send: `thrum send --to @agent --stdin <<'EOF'`
- Reply: `thrum reply <msg-id> --stdin <<'EOF'`
Run each send and reply above as ONE standalone command, with the heredoc as its only redirection.
Write any `--body-file` contents in a separate tool call.
Never chain with `&&`, `;` or `||`, or prefix `VAR=`, in the same command.
